    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass. `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a test helper), and both of its tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `contactPreference` derived field on the owner resource, following the same pattern the codebase already uses for other computed read-only fields (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, `displayName`).\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `contactPreference` and a `formatContactPreference` method that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner has a non-blank email, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`.\n\nBecause the mapping lives in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)`, it applies uniformly across every endpoint that serializes an owner (create, get, list, v1 and v2), matching how the other derived fields behave. I kept it a plain string rather than an OpenAPI enum to stay consistent with the existing `locality` field and avoid MapStruct enum-conversion complications.\n\nVerified: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `corePhoneWhenNoEmail` (expects `PHONE`) and `functionalityEmailWhenPresent` (expects `EMAIL`) both green, and the full `mvn test` build succeeds.",
