    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change follows the established structure of this mapper exactly:\n\n- `contactPreference` is a derived, read-only DTO field, so putting its logic in a `@Named` MapStruct formatter default method on `OwnerMapper` is the right unit \u2014 this is precisely how `formatLocality`, `formatMembershipLevel`, `formatMembershipNumber`, `formatDisplayName`, and `formatInitials` are all handled.\n- The `@Mapping` annotation is registered on `toOwnerDto` in the same block as its siblings, and the method is placed among the other formatters. Nothing is out of place.\n- The null-guard-then-derive shape and the `getEmail() != null && !getEmail().isBlank()` presence check mirror the surrounding formatters (the same email check already appears in `formatMembershipLevel`), so a maintainer would find it immediately familiar.\n- The OpenAPI schema addition mirrors the neighboring read-only derived fields (title/description/type/example/`readOnly: true`).\n\nOn the one point worth weighing \u2014 the `hasEmail` expression is now duplicated between `formatContactPreference` and `formatMembershipLevel` \u2014 extracting a shared helper would not fit this file's idiom, where each formatter is deliberately self-contained and inlines its own trivial checks. A one-line boolean does not warrant a shared abstraction here, and introducing one would be less natural than the duplication. No changes needed.",
